# synthetic-todo-goal.jsonl — HAND-WRITTEN, not a wire capture.
#
# `session/todoListChanged` and `session/goalChanged` are emitted by the real
# provider's own task tooling; the echo provider never emits either, and no
# capture in this directory contains one. So this file is written by hand, in
# the same `<-- ` frame format the real captures use, to exercise the three
# transitions the fold has to get right: a whole-list replace, an empty list
# (the card goes), and a goal that is set, updated past 100 %, and cleared with
# an explicit null.
#
# It then sets both again, because a cleared card has to be able to come back —
# and because that final state is the one the phase-4 screenshot shows.
#
# The `synthetic-` prefix is load-bearing: nothing here was ever on a wire, and
# it must never be read as evidence of what Muse does.
